{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:08:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_c5d217a3561b45b49252fb2e3251ce1a","id":"pg_0fc9fbcb6a46543c8699a5d9fcdd9ec2","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/matthewzmd-aidermacs-release-md-b9a2512e54d8-a5d9fcdd9ec2.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_48102cfc606e5eda92a8bb0c8d82315a"],"title":"MatthewZMD/aidermacs/RELEASE.md @ b9a2512e54d8","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:08:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c5d217a3561b45b49252fb2e3251ce1a"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0ea846dfafc022efcadfdaf9a68e6e6763d098849cd68043d04d8af306ebcd35"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Two terminal backends are supported: comint (default, Emacs built-in) and vterm (better terminal compatibility), selected via aidermacs-backend."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1034378ab56cd3e5f51ab4c07e8a18581c3f9cd74a9d4dbd472a4a5da5ec72b0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Dynamic model selection fetches available models from OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, Google Gemini, and OpenRouter, caching lists and filtering by Aider version and configured API keys; this applies only to solo (non-Architect) mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_242089bd9f1a8c425d4de35c076a89913d5f526e1a22f55b70a748b6373fd1f9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The aidermacs-before-run-backend-hook runs custom setup before the backend starts, using a copy of process-environment so secrets set there affect only the Aider backend."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2471b364d19ac56aaab526c979b55921072e6deed10a60f9ad1a7bcfa881fca8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Aidermacs began as a fork of aider.el and diverged to prioritize Emacs-native workflows, positioning itself as an Emacs-centric alternative to Cursor-style AI editors."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2677a720bb1448bf61bbed694956bd5c54bd6def8b63f9af5d74a49016d67c54"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Aidermacs wraps the external Aider tool (or its community fork aider-ce), requiring Emacs >= 26.1 and the Transient package."},{"claim_ids":["clm_308533db8848fcad6254185c0eec8bbda3f1668fdabbfe76d3911e848437f916"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Code added to a session is sent to the AI provider, so users should be mindful of sensitive code; Aider itself currently supports only Python 3.12."},{"claim_ids":["clm_367f3727173dababa023e618f5a83300600866e7b2b258ab2542615b977b281e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Auto-commits of AI-generated changes are disabled by default (unlike Aider's default), and can be re-enabled via aidermacs-auto-commits."},{"claim_ids":["clm_436eed0809f3078fda5c1f8df4ed1fe8f5f0188c63581f0151b78cfe215f07d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The main interface is a Magit-like transient menu, invoked via M-x aidermacs-transient-menu or a user-bound key such as C-c a."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4c19f6b27b7169c64643452cac603a1810d5798e267930bed6cf3b9eba4fe6eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Architect mode uses two models: an Architect model for reasoning and an Editor model for code generation; each can be configured independently via aidermacs-architect-model and aidermacs-editor-model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_67311ea0cf73b7f842afb894c9c41678f5f22508fd31abc6570fadb65f163f22"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration precedence: if an .aider.conf.yml is found it takes highest priority and Emacs variables are ignored; otherwise Emacs variables override environment variables, which override built-in defaults."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7ebb360c50dcfda4bd910cbe82c94a8c47be2624fbd81c7cb861cc80061a121a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The AI-comment file-watching feature (AI!/AI? triggers) currently only works in vterm mode, per the README note."},{"claim_ids":["clm_89ca7663f2395484efface4863a1bc2041df5f0b35472b076dc2c88546a3f66a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"When enabled, diff review captures pre-edit file state and shows changes through Emacs' built-in ediff interface for accept/reject review; controlled by aidermacs-show-diff-after-change (default t)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4433adc474f29a8b723ba3f2ba02d16ce504903142e31dc762a83a209ca6318"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Files added as editable grant the AI read and modify permission; any add-file command prefixed with C-u adds the file as read-only instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_be8740f7601d5d8ed98ef775a7a028f957053c003f3b76687a40f776bd2d9a5a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prompt history and a curated common-prompts list (aidermacs-common-prompts) are saved and available across all sessions via completion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c9d3f0afb2628ad5b3832e54778bcfd671394d9231bedbb9bfa5eb049650cf5c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default Aidermacs requires explicit confirmation before applying Architect-mode changes; setting aidermacs-auto-accept-architect to t enables automatic acceptance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cbfff34147ce070c4e830ea72ab64ae08f6538b8aa0a58e4a9fe087936c0eac8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The transient menu includes session commands (start/open, clear history, reset, exit), persistent mode toggles (Code, Chat/Ask, Architect, Help), utilities, file actions, and code actions, with 'All File Actions' and 'All Code Actions' submenus."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0ea846dfafc022efcadfdaf9a68e6e6763d098849cd68043d04d8af306ebcd35","clm_1034378ab56cd3e5f51ab4c07e8a18581c3f9cd74a9d4dbd472a4a5da5ec72b0","clm_242089bd9f1a8c425d4de35c076a89913d5f526e1a22f55b70a748b6373fd1f9","clm_2471b364d19ac56aaab526c979b55921072e6deed10a60f9ad1a7bcfa881fca8","clm_2677a720bb1448bf61bbed694956bd5c54bd6def8b63f9af5d74a49016d67c54","clm_308533db8848fcad6254185c0eec8bbda3f1668fdabbfe76d3911e848437f916","clm_367f3727173dababa023e618f5a83300600866e7b2b258ab2542615b977b281e","clm_436eed0809f3078fda5c1f8df4ed1fe8f5f0188c63581f0151b78cfe215f07d5","clm_4c19f6b27b7169c64643452cac603a1810d5798e267930bed6cf3b9eba4fe6eb","clm_67311ea0cf73b7f842afb894c9c41678f5f22508fd31abc6570fadb65f163f22","clm_7ebb360c50dcfda4bd910cbe82c94a8c47be2624fbd81c7cb861cc80061a121a","clm_89ca7663f2395484efface4863a1bc2041df5f0b35472b076dc2c88546a3f66a","clm_a4433adc474f29a8b723ba3f2ba02d16ce504903142e31dc762a83a209ca6318","clm_be8740f7601d5d8ed98ef775a7a028f957053c003f3b76687a40f776bd2d9a5a","clm_c9d3f0afb2628ad5b3832e54778bcfd671394d9231bedbb9bfa5eb049650cf5c","clm_cbfff34147ce070c4e830ea72ab64ae08f6538b8aa0a58e4a9fe087936c0eac8"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:08:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_c5d217a3561b45b49252fb2e3251ce1a","id":"pg_1b5c47838bbf5f80b247222dfd8e6080","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/matthewzmd-aiderma